{
 "schema": "godot3_isms/1",
 "verified_on": "2026-09-15",
 "verified_against": "Godot 4.7 class reference (docs 'stable' = 4.7), 4.7 branch source, upgrading_to_godot_4 guide",
 "regex_flags": "python re, compile with re.MULTILINE; apply per GDScript source file",
 "not_isms_do_not_flag": [
  "lerp(a, b, t) on Vector2/Vector3/Color and lerp_angle(from, to, weight) — valid @GlobalScope functions (https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_@globalscope.html)",
  "instance_from_id(id), is_instance_valid(obj), is_instance_id_valid(id) — valid globals (https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_@globalscope.html)",
  "randomize(), randi(), randf() — valid; note randomize() is now called automatically at startup (https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.html)",
  "get_node_or_null(path), has_node(path), %UniqueName access — valid Node API",
  "connect(\"sig\", callable) two-argument string form — valid (warn only, see connect_string_2arg)",
  "emit_signal(\"sig\", args) — valid (Object.emit_signal(signal: StringName, ...)); sig.emit() preferred (https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_object.html)",
  "Transform2D, Vector2/3/4, Basis, Plane, AABB, Rect2 — unchanged names",
  "await on a coroutine (a function that itself awaits) — valid"
 ],
 "rows": [
  {
   "id": "yield_call",
   "pattern": "\\byield\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "yield(obj, \"signal\") / var x = yield(f(), \"completed\")",
   "godot4_form": "await obj.signal / var x = await f()",
   "note": "`yield` is kept only as a reserved keyword for transition; it does not work. GDScript basics keyword table.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "yield_create_timer",
   "pattern": "\\byield\\s*\\(\\s*get_tree\\(\\)\\.create_timer\\(",
   "godot3_form": "yield(get_tree().create_timer(1.0), \"timeout\")",
   "godot4_form": "await get_tree().create_timer(1.0).timeout",
   "note": "SceneTree.create_timer(time_sec, process_always=true, process_in_physics=false, ignore_time_scale=false) returns SceneTreeTimer; await its `timeout` signal.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_scenetree.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "await_timer_without_timeout",
   "pattern": "\\bawait\\s+get_tree\\(\\)\\.create_timer\\([^)\\n]*\\)\\s*(#.*)?$",
   "godot3_form": "(hallucination) await get_tree().create_timer(1.0)",
   "godot4_form": "await get_tree().create_timer(1.0).timeout",
   "note": "hallucination: awaiting the SceneTreeTimer object itself does not wait (REDUNDANT_AWAIT warning); you must await the `timeout` signal.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_scenetree.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "connect_string_3arg",
   "pattern": "\\.connect\\s*\\(\\s*[\\\"'][^\\\"'\\n]+[\\\"']\\s*,\\s*[^,()\\n]+\\s*,\\s*[\\\"']",
   "godot3_form": "obj.connect(\"pressed\", self, \"_on_pressed\")",
   "godot4_form": "obj.pressed.connect(_on_pressed)  # or obj.connect(\"pressed\", Callable(self, \"_on_pressed\"))",
   "note": "Object.connect(signal: StringName, callable: Callable, flags: int = 0). The 3-argument (target, method-name) form no longer exists.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_object.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "connect_string_2arg",
   "pattern": "\\.connect\\s*\\(\\s*[\\\"'][^\\\"'\\n]+[\\\"']\\s*,\\s*[^,()\\n]+\\s*\\)",
   "godot3_form": "obj.connect(\"pressed\", callable)  (string-based, still valid)",
   "godot4_form": "obj.pressed.connect(callable)",
   "note": "Valid in Godot 4 but the upgrade guide recommends the Signal-based syntax so signal-name typos are caught at parse time.",
   "severity": "warn",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "disconnect_is_connected_3arg",
   "pattern": "\\.(disconnect|is_connected)\\s*\\(\\s*[\\\"'][^\\\"'\\n]+[\\\"']\\s*,\\s*[^,()\\n]+\\s*,\\s*[\\\"']",
   "godot3_form": "obj.disconnect(\"sig\", self, \"m\") / obj.is_connected(\"sig\", self, \"m\")",
   "godot4_form": "obj.sig.disconnect(m) / obj.sig.is_connected(m)",
   "note": "Object.disconnect(signal: StringName, callable: Callable); is_connected(signal, callable).",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_object.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "signal_any_hallucination",
   "pattern": "\\bSignal\\.any\\s*\\(|\\bawait\\s+[\\w.$]+\\.any\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "(hallucination) await Signal.any([a, b])",
   "godot4_form": "await a  # Signal has no any(); await one signal, or write a small aggregator node/lambda",
   "note": "hallucination: Signal's methods are connect, disconnect, emit, get_connections, get_name, get_object, get_object_id, has_connections, is_connected, is_null. No any()/wait().",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_signal.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "signal_wait_hallucination",
   "pattern": "\\bawait\\s+[\\w.$]+\\.wait\\s*\\(\\s*\\)",
   "godot3_form": "(hallucination) await sig.wait()",
   "godot4_form": "await sig",
   "note": "hallucination: Signal has no wait(); `await signal` is the whole syntax. (May be a false positive if a user coroutine is literally named wait.)",
   "severity": "warn",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_signal.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "funcref",
   "pattern": "\\bfuncref\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "funcref(self, \"method\")",
   "godot4_form": "Callable(self, \"method\")  # or just self.method",
   "note": "Callable(object: Object, method: StringName) constructor; methods are first-class Callables in Godot 4.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_callable.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "thread_start_string",
   "pattern": "\\.start\\s*\\(\\s*self\\s*,\\s*[\\\"']",
   "godot3_form": "thread.start(self, \"_work\", data)",
   "godot4_form": "thread.start(_work.bind(data))",
   "note": "Threading syntax changed to Callable-based start().",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "tween_node_3x",
   "pattern": "\\.interpolate_property\\s*\\(|\\btween_all_completed\\b|\\btween_completed\\b",
   "godot3_form": "$Tween.interpolate_property(...); $Tween.start(); yield($Tween, \"tween_all_completed\")",
   "godot4_form": "var t := create_tween(); t.tween_property(obj, \"prop\", final_val, dur); await t.finished",
   "note": "The Tween node was removed in favor of Tweeners (Tween.tween_property(object, property: NodePath, final_val, duration: float)); Tween signals are finished, step_finished, loop_finished.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "idle_frame",
   "pattern": "\\bidle_frame\\b",
   "godot3_form": "yield(get_tree(), \"idle_frame\")",
   "godot4_form": "await get_tree().process_frame",
   "note": "SceneTree signals in 4.x are process_frame and physics_frame (idle_frame was the 3.x name).",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_scenetree.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "super_dot_call",
   "pattern": "^\\s*\\.\\s*_?\\w+\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "._ready()  (call parent implementation)",
   "godot4_form": "super()  # or super._ready()",
   "note": "Lifecycle functions no longer implicitly call the parent; use super(). The leading-dot call syntax is gone.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "instance_call",
   "pattern": "\\.instance\\s*\\(\\s*\\)",
   "godot3_form": "packed_scene.instance()",
   "godot4_form": "packed_scene.instantiate()",
   "note": "PackedScene.instance() -> instantiate(). (The 3-to-4 converter handles this with a custom rule.)",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "change_scene",
   "pattern": "\\.change_scene(_to)?\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "get_tree().change_scene(path) / change_scene_to(packed)",
   "godot4_form": "get_tree().change_scene_to_file(path) / change_scene_to_packed(packed)",
   "note": "SceneTree has change_scene_to_file(path: String), change_scene_to_packed(packed_scene), change_scene_to_node(); no change_scene()/change_scene_to().",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_scenetree.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "object_instance_from_id",
   "pattern": "\\bObject\\.instance_from_id\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "(hallucination) Object.instance_from_id(id)",
   "godot4_form": "instance_from_id(id)  # global function; also is_instance_id_valid(id)",
   "note": "instance_from_id(instance_id: int) -> Object is an @GlobalScope function in both 3.x and 4.x; it is not a static method on Object. Plain `instance_from_id(...)` must NOT be flagged.",
   "severity": "warn",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_@globalscope.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "kinematicbody",
   "pattern": "\\bKinematicBody(2D)?\\b",
   "godot3_form": "extends KinematicBody2D / KinematicBody",
   "godot4_form": "extends CharacterBody2D / CharacterBody3D",
   "note": "Renamed in 4.0.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "move_and_slide_args",
   "pattern": "\\bmove_and_slide\\s*\\(\\s*[^)\\s][^)]*\\)",
   "godot3_form": "velocity = move_and_slide(velocity, Vector2.UP)",
   "godot4_form": "velocity = v  # property\nmove_and_slide()  # no args, returns bool",
   "note": "CharacterBody2D.move_and_slide() takes no arguments and uses/modifies the `velocity` property (same for CharacterBody3D). up_direction is a property.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_characterbody2d.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "move_and_slide_assign",
   "pattern": "\\bvelocity\\s*=\\s*move_and_slide\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "velocity = move_and_slide(velocity)",
   "godot4_form": "move_and_slide()  # velocity is updated in place",
   "note": "move_and_slide() returns bool (collided), not the new velocity.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_characterbody2d.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "move_and_slide_with_snap",
   "pattern": "\\bmove_and_slide_with_snap\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "move_and_slide_with_snap(velocity, snap, up)",
   "godot4_form": "move_and_slide()  # snapping via floor_snap_length property",
   "note": "Not present in the 4.x CharacterBody2D API; floor_snap_length is a CharacterBody2D property (verified in 4.7 source).",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_characterbody2d.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "get_slide_count",
   "pattern": "\\.get_slide_count\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "get_slide_count()",
   "godot4_form": "get_slide_collision_count()",
   "note": "CharacterBody2D/3D.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.7/editor/project_upgrade/renames_map_3_to_4.cpp"
  },
  {
   "id": "rigidbody_add_force",
   "pattern": "\\.(add_force|add_central_force|add_torque)\\s*\\(",
   "godot3_form": "add_force(offset, force) / add_central_force(f) / add_torque(t)",
   "godot4_form": "apply_force(force, position=Vector2.ZERO) / apply_central_force(f) / apply_torque(t)",
   "note": "Renamed; note apply_force takes (force, position) — the 3.x add_force took (offset, force). add_constant_force/add_constant_central_force exist in 4.x for persistent forces.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_rigidbody2d.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "apply_impulse_order",
   "pattern": "\\.apply_impulse\\s*\\(\\s*[^,()\\n]+,\\s*[^,()\\n]+\\)",
   "godot3_form": "apply_impulse(offset, impulse)",
   "godot4_form": "apply_impulse(impulse, position=Vector2(0, 0))",
   "note": "Argument order swapped between 3.x (offset, impulse) and 4.x (impulse, position). Two-argument calls need a manual check.",
   "severity": "warn",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_rigidbody2d.html"
  },
  {
   "id": "rigidbody_mode",
   "pattern": "\\.mode\\s*=\\s*(RigidBody2D|RigidBody3D|RigidBody)\\.MODE_\\w+|\\bMODE_(RIGID|STATIC|CHARACTER|KINEMATIC)\\b",
   "godot3_form": "body.mode = RigidBody2D.MODE_STATIC",
   "godot4_form": "body.freeze = true; body.freeze_mode = RigidBody2D.FREEZE_MODE_STATIC",
   "note": "RigidBody2D/3D have no `mode` property in 4.x; use freeze + freeze_mode.",
   "severity": "error",
   "source_url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_rigidbody2d.html"
  },
  {
